  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 130 AM CDT Sun Oct 4 2026\n\nDry conditions and seasonable temperatures continue today. A dry\ncold front provides reinforcing northerly flow and some high\nclouds this morning. High pressure pushes eastward through the\nMidwest early week, with a ridge axis moving through Tuesday.\nThe high eventually sets up to our east mid-late week, which\nwill allow for a more southerly component to winds locally.\nTemperatures slowly warm mid to late week with southerly flow\nwith late week highs into the 80s.\n\nModels are in strong alignment on dry conditions through at\nleast Friday. Precipitation chances only return next weekend,\nwith models favoring the Deep South for rain chances but\ndiffering strongly on the type of system, so continued\nmonitoring will be needed.",
